messages:    1%|          | 2/204 [00:00<00:39,  5.17it/s][['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B or C. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nNo students who work in the library are from the computer science department. All students who have part-time jobs offered by the university are students who work in the library. All students who take the database course are from the computer science department. All students instructed by professor David are taking the database course. All students working in the lab are instructed by professor David. James is a student working in the lab. Jack neither has a part-time job offered by the university nor works in the lab.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, is the following statement true, false, or uncertain? James either takes the database course or has a part-time job offered by the university.\n# Options:\nA) True\nB) False\nC) Uncertain', '<think>.\nTo determine if the statement "James either takes the database course or has a part-time job offered by the university" is true, false, or uncertain, let\'s analyze the given information step by step:.\n\n1.**No students who work in the library are from the computer science department.**.\n   - This means if a student works in the library, they cannot be from the computer science department.\n\n2.**All students who have part-time jobs offered by the university are students who work in the library.**.\n   - This implies that if a student has a part-time job, they must work in the library.\n\n3.**All students who take the database course are from the computer science department.**.\n   - This means if a student takes the database course, they must be from the computer science department.\n\n4.**All students instructed by professor David are taking the database course.**.\n   - This means if a student is instructed by professor David, they are taking the database course.\n\n5.**All students working in the lab are instructed by professor David.**.\n   - This means if a student works in the lab, they are instructed by professor David and thus taking the database course.\n\n6.**James is a student working in the lab.**.\n   - From point 5, since James works in the lab, he is instructed by professor David and therefore taking the database course.Jack both has a part-time job offered by the university and works in the lab.. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
