messages:  [['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B or C. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nIf George likes music, he wants to compose. If George has access to a program, he can compose. If George can compose and wants to compose, he will compose.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, is the following statement true, false, or uncertain? If George will not compose, George can not compose.\n# Options:\nA) True\nB) False\nC) Uncertain', '<think>.\nTo solve this logical reasoning problem, let\'s break down the given information and analyze the statement step by step.\n\n1.**Understanding the Given Information:**.\n   - If George likes music, he wants to compose.\n   - If George has access to a program, he can compose.\n   - If George can compose and wants to compose, he will compose.\n\n2.**Analyzing the Statement:**.\n   - The statement to evaluate is: "If George will not compose, George can not compose.".\n\n3.**Logical Analysis:**.\n   - From the given information, we know that if George wants to compose, he will compose.This can be written as:.\n     \\[.\n     \\text{If George wants to compose, then George will compose.}.\n     \\].\n   - We also know that if George has access to a program, he can compose.This can be written as:.\n     \\[.\n     \\text{If George has access to a program, then George can compose.}.\n     \\].\n\n4.**Considering the Statement:**.\n   - The statement "If George will not compose, George can not compose" can be written as:.\n     \\[.\n     \\text{If George will not compose, then George can not compose.}.\n     \\].If George will compose, George can compose.. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
