messages:  [['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B or C. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nAll mammals are animals. All monkeys are mammals. An animal is either a monkey or a bird. All birds fly. All animals breathe. If something can fly, then it has wings. If Rock is neither a fly nor a bird, then Rock neither flies nor breathes.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, is the following statement true, false, or uncertain? Rock is a monkey.\n# Options:\nA) True\nB) False\nC) Uncertain', '<think>.\nTo determine whether the statement "Rock is a monkey" is true, false, or uncertain based on the given context, let\'s break down the information step by step:.\n\n1.**All mammals are animals.**.\n   - This establishes a direct relationship between mammals and animals.\n\n2.**All monkeys are mammals.**.\n   - This means that any monkey falls under the category of mammals.\n\n3.**An animal is either a monkey or a bird.**.\n   - This categorizes animals into two distinct groups: monkeys and birds.\n\n4.**All birds fly.**.\n   - This tells us that any bird has the ability to fly.\n\n5.**All animals breathe.**.\n   - This establishes that any animal has the ability to breathe.\n\n6.**If Rock is neither a fly nor a bird, then Rock neither flies nor breathes.**.\n   - This statement provides a conditional relationship between Rock and the ability to fly and breathe.If Rock meets the criteria for being a fly or a bird, it can fly and therefore breathe.\n\nNow, let\'s analyze the statement "Rock is not a monkey":.\n\n- From the context, we know that monkeys are not mammals.\n- We also know that not all animals breathe.\n- However, the statement "Rock is not a monkey" does not provide any information about Rock\'s inability to fly or its classification as a bird.\n\nGiven the information:.\n- Rock is explicitly stated to be a monkey and explicitly excluded from being a monkey.\n- The conditional statement about Rock\'s flying and breathing does provide enough information to definitively determine Rock\'s classification.\n\nTherefore, based on the given context, the statement "Rock is not a monkey" is certain.\n\n<｜Assistant｜> <answer>\n. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
