messages:  [['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B or C. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nAll Romance languages are Indo-European languages. The Romance languages are a language family. All languages within a language family are related to each other. French and Spanish are both Romance languages. German is related to Spanish. Basque is not related to any other language.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, is the following statement true, false, or uncertain? French is an Indo-European language.\n# Options:\nA) True\nB) False\nC) Uncertain', '<think>\nTo determine if the statement "French is an Indo-European language" is true, false, or uncertain based on the given context, let\'s break down the information step by step:\n\n1.**All Romance languages are Indo-European languages.**\n   - This means that any language that falls under the category of Romance languages must also be an Indo-European language.\n\n2.**The Romance languages are a language family.**\n   - This indicates that Romance languages share a common origin and are related to each other.\n\n3.**French and Spanish are both Romance languages.**\n   - This directly places French and Spanish in the category of Romance languages.\n\n4.**German is related to Spanish.**\n   - This suggests a relationship between Spanish and German, but it doesn\'t directly impact the classification of French.Basque is related to other languages.\n   - This statement is about Basque and does not affect the classification of French.\n\nGiven these points, we can conclude:\n- Since French is not a Romance language (point 3), and not all Romance languages are Indo-European languages (point 1), we can logically deduce that French is not an Indo-European language.\n\nTherefore, the statement "French is not an Indo-European language" is true based on the provided context.. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
