messages:   43%|####3     | 88/204 [04:50<02:38,  1.37s/it][['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B or C. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nIf people are twins or triplets, then they spend a lot of time hanging out with and playing with their siblings. If people have siblings who are the same age, then they are twins or triplets. If people complain often about annoying siblings, then they have siblings who are the same age. If people do not live at home regularly, then they do not develop strong bonds with their family members. If people spend a lot of time hanging out with and playing with their siblings, then they often did not live at home regularly. Luke is either both a twin or triplet and develops strong bonds with his family members, or he neither is a twin or triplet nor develops strong bonds with his family members.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, is the following statement true, false, or uncertain? Luke is neither a twin nor triplet nor complains often about annoying siblings.\n# Options:\nA) True\nB) False\nC) Uncertain', '<think>\nTo solve this logical reasoning problem, let\'s break down the given information and analyze it step by step to determine the truth of the statement "Luke is neither a twin nor triplet nor complains often about annoying siblings."\n\n1.**Condition 1:** If people are twins or triplets, then they spend a lot of time hanging out with and playing with their siblings.\n   - This implies that if Luke is a twin or triplet, he would spend a lot of time with his siblings.\n\n2.**Condition 2:** If people have siblings who are the same age, then they are twins or triplets.\n   - This means that if Luke has siblings who are the same age, he must be a twin or triplet.\n\n3.**Condition 3:** If people complain often about annoying siblings, then they have siblings who are the same age.\n   - This implies that if Luke complains often about annoying siblings, he must have siblings who are the same age, which means he is a twin or triplet.\n\n4.**Condition 4:** If people do not live at home regularly, then they do not develop strong bonds with their family members.\n   - This means that if Luke does not live at home regularly, he would not develop strong bonds with his family members.\n\n5.**Condition 5:** If people spend a lot of time hanging out with and playing with their siblings, then they often did not live at home regularly.\n   - This implies that if Luke spends a lot of time with his siblings, he would not live at home regularly.\n\n6.**Given Information:** Luke is either both a twin or triplet and develops strong bonds with his family members, or he neither is a twin or triplet nor develops strong bonds with his family members.\n   - This gives us two possible scenarios:\n     a. Luke is a twin or triplet and develops strong bonds with his family members.\n     b. Luke is neither a twin or triplet nor develops strong bonds with his family members.\n\nNow, let\'s analyze the statement "Luke is neither a twin nor triplet nor complains often about annoying siblings."\nLuke is either a twin or triplet and complains often about annoying siblings.. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
