R \\rightarrow L \\), if \\( R \\) is true, then \\( L \\) (being listed in Yelp's recommendations) must be true.\n     - From \\( L \\rightarrow \\neg N \\), if \\( L \\) is true, then \\( N \\) must be false.\n\n4. **Conclusion:**\n   - The statement \\( (T \\land N) \\rightarrow (R \\land \\neg T) \\) cannot be true because:\n     - If \\( T \\land N \\) is true, then \\( N \\) is true, which contradicts \\( R \\rightarrow \\neg N \\) (if \\( R \\) is true, \\( N \\) must be false).\n     - Therefore, the statement is logically inconsistent with the given premises.\n\nThus, the statement is **false**.\n\nThe correct answer is: **B) False**.\n</think>\n<answer>B) False</answer>",
