messages:  [['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B or C. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nAll employees who schedule a meeting with their customers will appear in the company today. Everyone who has lunch in the company schedules meetings with their customers. Employees will either have lunch in the company or have lunch at home. If an employee has lunch at home, then he/she is working remotely from home. All employees who are in other countries work remotely from home. No managers work remotely from home. James is either a manager and appears in the company today or neither a manager nor appears in the company today.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, is the following statement true, false, or uncertain? James has lunch in the company.\n# Options:\nA) True\nB) False\nC) Uncertain', '<think>\nTo determine if the statement "James has lunch in the company" is true, false, or uncertain, let\'s break down the given information and analyze it step by step:\n\n1.**All employees who schedule a meeting with their customers will appear in the company today.**\n   - This means if an employee schedules a meeting with their customers, they must be present in the company.\n\n2.**Everyone who has lunch in the company schedules meetings with their customers.**\n   - This implies that if an employee has lunch in the company, they must have scheduled a meeting with their customers.\n\n3.**Employees will either have lunch in the company or have lunch at home.**\n   - This establishes a binary choice for lunch locations.\n\n4.**If an employee has lunch at home, then he/she is working remotely from home.**\n   - This indicates that having lunch at home implies working remotely.\n\n5.**All employees who are in other countries work remotely from home.**\n   - This means if an employee is in another country, they are working remotely from home.\n\n6.**No managers work remotely from home.**\n   - This means if an employee is a manager, they cannot be working remotely from home.\n\n7.**James is either a manager and appears in the company today or neither a manager nor appears in the company today.**\n   - This gives us two possible scenarios for James:\n     - Scenario 1: James is a manager and appears in the company today.\n     - Scenario 2: James is not a manager and does not appear in the company today.\n\nNow, let\'s analyze each scenario:\n\nJames is not a manager and does not appear in the company today, he does not have lunch at home.. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
