messages:  [['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B or C. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nOn some Mondays at 8 pm, roses are given out on TV. Every rose given out on TV is on the Bachelor. Everything on the Bachelor portrays the lives of real people. All shows portraying the lives of real people are reality TV shows. Breaking Bad is not a reality TV show.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, is the following statement true, false, or uncertain? Breaking Bad is on Monday at 8 pm.\n# Options:\nA) True\nB) False\nC) Uncertain', '<think>.\nTo determine whether the statement "Breaking Bad is on Monday at 8 pm" is true, false, or uncertain based on the given context, let\'s break down the information step by step:.\n\n1.**Context Information:**.\n   - On some Mondays at 8 pm, roses are given out on TV.\n   - Every rose given out on TV is on the Bachelor.\n   - Everything on the Bachelor portrays the lives of real people.\n   - All shows portraying the lives of real people are reality TV shows.\n   - Breaking Bad is not a reality TV show.\n\n2.**Analyzing the Information:**.\n   - The context mentions that roses are given out on TV on some Mondays at 8 pm.\n   - These roses are on the Bachelor.\n   - The Bachelor portrays the lives of real people.\n   - Since the Bachelor is a reality TV show, and all shows portraying the lives of real people are reality TV shows, the Bachelor must be a reality TV show.In reality, Breaking Bad is a reality TV show, and it airs on Mondays at 8 pm.. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
