messages:  [['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B or C. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\n"Stranger Things" is a popular Netflix show. If a Netflix show is popular, Karen will binge-watch it. If and only if Karen binge-watches a Netflix show, she will download it. Karen does not download "Black Mirror". "Black Mirror" is a Netflix show. If Karen binge-watches a Netflix show, she will share it to Lisa.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, is the following statement true, false, or uncertain? "Black Mirror" is popular.\n# Options:\nA) True\nB) False\nC) Uncertain', '<think>.\nTo determine if the statement "Black Mirror is popular" is true, false, or uncertain based on the given context, let\'s break down the information step by step:.\n\n1.**"Stranger Things" is a popular Netflix show.**.\n   - This is given directly in the context.\n\n2.**If a Netflix show is popular, Karen will binge-watch it.**.\n   - This means that if "Stranger Things" is popular, Karen will binge-watch it.\n\n3.**If and only if Karen binge-watches a Netflix show, she will download it.**.\n   - This establishes a biconditional relationship between Karen binge-watching a show and downloading it.\n\n4.**Karen does not download "Black Mirror".**.\n   - This means that Karen does not binge-watch "Black Mirror" because if she did, she would download it.\n\n5.**"Black Mirror" is a Netflix show.**.\nIf Karen binge-watches a Netflix show, she will not share it to Lisa.. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
