messages:  [['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B or C. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nOn some Mondays at 8 pm, roses are given out on TV. Every rose given out on TV is on the Bachelor. Everything on the Bachelor portrays the lives of real people. All shows portraying the lives of real people are reality TV shows. Breaking Bad is not a reality TV show.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, is the following statement true, false, or uncertain? Breaking Bad is a TV show in which roses are given out on Monday at 8 pm.\n# Options:\nA) True\nB) False\nC) Uncertain', "<think>.\nTo solve this logical reasoning problem, let's break down the given information and analyze it step by step:.\n\n1.**Context Analysis:**.\n   - On some Mondays at 8 pm, roses are given out on TV.\n   - Every rose given out on TV is on the Bachelor.\n   - Everything on the Bachelor portrays the lives of real people.\n   - All shows portraying the lives of real people are reality TV shows.\n   - Breaking Bad is not a reality TV show.\n\n2.**Logical Deductions:**.\n   - Since Breaking Bad is not a reality TV show, it cannot be on the Bachelor (because everything on the Bachelor portrays the lives of real people).Breaking Bad is not a TV show in which roses are given out on Monday at 8 pm.. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
