messages:  [['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B or C. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nMonkeypox is an infectious disease caused by the monkeypox virus. Monkeypox virus can occur in certain animals, including humans. Humans are mammals. Mammals are animals. Symptons of Monkeypox include fever, headache, muscle pains, feeling tired, and so on. People feel tired when they get a glu.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, is the following statement true, false, or uncertain? There is an animal.\n# Options:\nA) True\nB) False\nC) Uncertain', '<think>\nTo determine if the statement "There is an animal" is true, false, or uncertain based on the given context, let\'s break down the information provided and analyze it step by step.\n\n1.**Monkeypox is an infectious disease caused by the monkeypox virus.**\n   - This tells us that monkeypox is a disease that can be caused by a virus.\n\n2.**Monkeypox virus can occur in certain animals, including humans.**\n   - This indicates that the monkeypox virus can be found in animals, and humans are mentioned as one of those animals.\n\n3.**Humans are mammals.**\n   - This establishes a relationship between humans and mammals.\n\n4.**Mammals are animals.**\n   - This clarifies that mammals are a subset of animals.\n\n5.**Symptoms of Monkeypox include fever, headache, muscle pains, feeling tired, and so on.There is no animal.. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
