messages:  [['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B or C. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nMonkeypox is an infectious disease caused by the monkeypox virus. Monkeypox virus can occur in certain animals, including humans. Humans are mammals. Mammals are animals. Symptons of Monkeypox include fever, headache, muscle pains, feeling tired, and so on. People feel tired when they get a glu.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, is the following statement true, false, or uncertain? No one gets flu.\n# Options:\nA) True\nB) False\nC) Uncertain', '<think>.\nTo determine whether the statement "No one gets flu" is true, false, or uncertain based on the given context, let\'s break down the information provided and analyze it step by step.\n\n1.**Context Analysis**:.\n   - Monkeypox is an infectious disease caused by the monkeypox virus.\n   - Monkeypox virus can occur in certain animals, including humans.\n   - Humans are mammals.\n   - Mammals are animals.\n   - Symptoms of Monkeypox include fever, headache, muscle pains, feeling tired, and so on.\n   - People feel tired when they get a fever.\n\n2.**Key Points**:.\n   - The context does not mention anything about the flu.\n   - The context only discusses monkeypox and its symptoms.\n   - The statement "No one gets flu" is not directly addressed or implied by the given information.\n\n3.**Flu Information**:.\n   - The flu (influenza) is a different infectious disease caused by the influenza virus.\n   - The flu can affect humans and is a common respiratory illness.Everyone gets the flu.. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
