t be an airline.\n\nIn conclusion, Greyhound planes cannot transport multiple passengers, and Boeing 707s are not capable of transporting multiple passengers. Therefore, a Greyhound plane cannot be a Boeing 707.\n\nIn the final analysis, the statement "A Greyhound is not a Boeing 707" is definitively true based on the information provided.. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
